reviews={
'test_tranche3_advanced_relational_nfs.py':'Full 602 lines. Twenty-five examples spanning nest/unnest, FD schemas, screens versus declared JD theories, temporal exact-time join, synthesis, GYO and antichains. Positive PNF round trip is real for one supplied projection, while claimed nonpartition loss retains every tuple in a grouping and never checks loss. EKNF examples assert implementation classification but do not independently establish elementary-key theory. 6NF/DKNF tests correctly retain Unsupported-style screens without complete theories; trivial supplied covers cannot establish completeness of all dependencies. RFNF key-cover tests distinguish key implication; ETNF alleged strict separation actually asserts all three forms true on the same schema. BCNF decomposition checks child BCNF only, not lossless reconstruction; minimal-cover permutation test checks deterministic output on five shuffles, not universal unique minimal covers. Exact parity relation independently produces 8 joins from 4 tuples, useful. GYO positive/negative hypergraphs and pairwise join example are bounded; Rissanen check merely verifies FD attribute containment, IND cycle check merely excludes one direct edge, FK cochain label is set inclusion with no complex/differential. No original imports/execution.',
'test_tranche4_streaming_and_sketches.py':'Full 966 lines in three contiguous displayed chunks. All sketch classes are test-local. Integer Count-Min updates are conservative only for nonnegative updates and compatible hashes; width/depth/seed validity not enforced, merge accepts different salts and reconstructs default seed. C039 confirms count7 becomes0 merging same-seed1 sketch with empty. Cuckoo insertion evicts using Python integer hash but lookup uses SHA-derived alternate index; C040 finds successful insertion makes admitted keys unfindable. Sparse HLL transition/commutative max register example is real; its identity assertion compares the same merge computation to itself and associativity is absent. T-digest error tests use uniform grids and normalized value error, not arbitrary-distribution rank bounds. Reservoir2000runs, HLL one cardinality, Bloom100members/nonmembers, Count-Min3keys+500noise and Space-Saving one ordered stream are samples, not probability guarantees. Median test sorts every window despite heap description. Sliding/tumbling sum, watermark max, tombstone overwrite and signed Counter cancellation are exact local examples; session merge does not test associativity, delta-join case has empty cross-delta intersection, and outer join emissions are handwritten. DGIM uses only one window-length stream so no real expiry case; no generated value-object strict-type controls despite headline. No production streaming implementation is exercised.'}
for name,s in reviews.items():a.record(b+name,1,len(a.source(b+name)),s)
